 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(N_f \cdot \frac{1}{C} \cdot R)$, where $N_f$ is the number of faces, $C$ is the chunk size, and $R$ is the rasterization cost per chunk (proportional to texture resolution) [G]. The overhead of chunking is minimal if $C$ is large enough to amortize API calls.
-- **Memory Complexity**: $O(H \cdot W \cdot 4 + C \cdot \text{rasterizer\_overhead})$. The dominant memory consumer is the output texture $(H, W, 4)$ [G]. Chunking limits the peak memory usage of the rasterizer's internal buffers.
